1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. Qe2 { Before looking at 4.d3 let's check something akin to a Worrall attack. } Bc5 5. c3 { -KEY- } O-O 6. d3 h6 { This move has Kramnik's stamp of approval. } 7. Nbd2 d6 8. h3 { White didn't castle, he wants to push g4 and it could be quite dangerous if we are not careful. } a6 9. Ba4 b5 10. Bc2 Ne7 $1 { The simplest solution. Black discourages any g2-g4 plan in view of ...Ng6-f4. } 11. d4 exd4 12. cxd4 Bb6 $11 { I would say Black is more comfortable with ...Ng6 and ...Re8. } 
