[Result "*"]

1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. Bb5 Nf6 4. d4 { A relatively rare way of omitting the main Berlin lines. As we will see, the play is likely to transpose to one of the subvariations of the classical ...a6 Ruy Lopez. -KEY- } exd4 5. e5 Ne4 $1 { It's important to remember that the knight is placed better on e4 rather than on d5 because it has access to the always useful c5-square. } 6. O-O a6 { The simplest way to achieve good play is to chase White's Spanish bishop. } 7. Ba4 Nc5 8. Bxc6 $6 dxc6 9. Nxd4 Ne6 { is a worse version of the 7. Bxc6, 9. Re1 line for White. The rook is still on f1. } 
 *

